  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 329 AM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nToday through Wednesday:\n\nHot and dry conditions are expected ahead of Hurricane Isaias \napproach to the Gulf coast. Breezy conditions combined with hot/dry \nconditions in place, there is a potential for fire weather concerns \nthrough Friday for the northern portions of the area. \n\nHurricane Isaias continues to move in the central Gulf, eventually \nturning northward towards the AL/FL coastline over the next couple \nof days. Center of circulation will remain east of the CWA, keeping \ngreatest impacts out of the area. Locally, possible impacts from \nIsaias will be flash flooding (2-4 in of rainfall over a short \nperiod) along and east of I-55 starting Friday night through \nSaturday night. Wind gusts of 30-40 mph will be also possible within \nthe Friday night-Saturday night timeframe for areas east of I-55. As \nIsaias progress closer, additional updates will be provided so \nplease remain up to date with the latest information.  \n\nOnce the remnants of Isaias progress away from the area, hot and dry \nconditions will return as high pressure builds over the region. /SW/",
